sentences.t:
Dardanus, Iliacae primus pater urbis et auctor,
Electra, ut Grai perhibent, Atlantide cretus,
advehitur Teucros;

sentences.l:
Dardanus, of the Ilian first father city and founder,
born of Electra, as the Greeks report, Atlas's daughter,
is carried to the Teucrians;

Electra, mightiest Atlas
brought forth, who the heavenly on his shoulder holds up spheres;
to you Mercury is father, whom bright Maia
on Cyllene's cold, conceived, peak bore;

sentences.t:
Hic spelunca fuit, vasto summota recessu,
semihominis Caci facies quam dira tenebat
solis inaccessam radiis;

sentences.l:
Here a cave was, in a vast withdrawn recess,
which of half-human Cacus the shape, dreadful, held,
to the sun's unreachable rays;
